# Root build-context excludes for backend image builds.
#
# The backend build context is the PROJECT ROOT (docker-compose.yml
# `context: ..` and infra/stack.py `from_asset("../")`), and the backend
# Dockerfiles do `COPY . ./iris`, so without this file the entire tree —
# including .venv/ and venv/ (~1.7GB) — is shipped into the daemon.
#
# This list mirrors the CDK asset `exclude` in infra/stack.py so local
# (docker-compose) builds and the CDK/AgentCore build stay consistent.
# Do NOT add codebase_artifacts/ or config_docker.yaml here — the non-S3
# backend image copies codebase_artifacts/ and every image renames
# config_docker.yaml to config.yaml at build time.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/cdk.out
infra/cdk.out
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
*.log
